Sectional groups:-

- Aim: Represent the interests of a particular group within society can represent their Civil Rights
- Examples: Muslim Councils of Britain, National Union of Students, Trade Unions E.g. - RMT for train stuff

Cause groups:-

- Aim: Promote a particular cause/issue
- Examples: Friends of the Earth or Liberty

Insider Groups:-

Consulted by the government: Yes
Access to government power: Yes
Sectional Groups or Cause Groups: Sectional
Examples: British Medical Association, Howard League for Penal reform

Outersider Groups:-


Consulted by the government: No
Access to government power: No
Sectional Groups or Cause Groups: Cause
Examples: Extinction Rebellion, Just Stop Oil
Outsider by necessity: They are too controversial and can’t be spoken to government
Ideological Outsiders: groups that believe a different things to the government - e.g. Adam Smith institute - Margaret Thatcher loved them so they became insiders but after lost this status
